  "problem": "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}-{y}^{\u2032}-2y=6,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(3)={e}^{6},\\,{y}^{\u2032}(4)={e}^{8},\\,3\\le x\\le 4\n$$\n\nThe solution is given by\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-x}+g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the constants $A$ and $B,$ and the function $g(x).$\n\n$\\,A=$ {{field-1}} \n$\\,B=$ \n{{field-2}} $\\,g(x)=$ {{field-3}}",
